## RESEARCH ARTICLE
A lantern-like $[Z\mathsf{n}_{116}]$ cage consisted of six $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{14}{\mathsf{O}}_{21}]$ and eight $[Z n_{4}{\mathsf{O}}_{4}]$ clusters represents the highest nuclearity nanocage assembled by $z_{n}$ -clusters to date. It is the first eco-friendly noble-metal-free MOFs catalyst for the cyclization of propargylic amines with $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ . The DFT calculations uncovered $Z n(11)$ can efficiently activate $C\equiv0$ bonds and $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ , and the electronic properties of intermediates and products can help to understand the reaction mechanism.
